A||N||15||Seanh||Can't get the damn cat converter out!||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||06-06-2001||06:49 PM||||I am currently in the process of replacing my cat converter with a straight pipe. I have the correct pipe, but can't get the damn converter off my exhaust. Mine is obviously not stock, and has been replaced once or more. It is only clamped on, so I thought it would easy, but no! Anyway, I have pounded for hours on that thing and it won't budge. Iv sprayed gobs of penatrating oil on it, and am still waiting it out. Anyone got any good ideas to getting this stupid thing off? Maybe I should just drive around until it falls off  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ? Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||stsmithgt||06-06-2001||06:57 PM||||"ASSUMING" the cat pipe goes over the ends that lead to the rest of the system, using a mini grinder to cut a spit on both sides of the "cats" pipe so it can have expansion room to pull the other pipe out with minimal damage.  If there're already expansion type splits, maybe a heavy duty stiff putty knife can be jammed in there to separate them or at least allow the penetration oil to get in further.  Since I don't know the cituation, I'm just blowing smoke out my..., but it might give you an idea anyway.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 06-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||06-06-2001||07:01 PM||||The way this cat is in there is really screwed up, looks like it has been replaced so many times there running out of pipe. One side of the cat goes over the pipe comming from the engine, but the other end goes inside the pipe going to the muffler. Still not a bad idea, I just wish I had a mini grinder. I have giganticly huge grider we use to clean the tanks on our pontoon boat, but I don't even think it would fit under the Fiero, much less enough room to operate it. <P>I was thinking it might come out with some heat, so maybe start and run the car for a few minutes and warm it up, then go pound on it for a while longer.||||reg||1
Z||000003||starfighter007@msn.com||06-06-2001||08:07 PM||||do you have access to a sawsall otherwise known as a recipricating saw?If you drive it around to heat up Ido not think you will get it hot enough to do what you want to do.If you dont have access to any of the mentioned tools.you will and should have taken it to a local muffler shop give them $40.00and have them done it in about 30 minutes hope this helps you some what good luck||||reg||3
Z||000004||Bluebottlejunky||06-06-2001||08:10 PM||||hmmm, id use the mini grinder if you can it worked great on mine..when the last person clamped it on..they made a huge lip!<P>------------------<BR>Hello, My name is Mike and I am addicted too fiero's...PLEASE dont help me.<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||4
