Z||000013||MooCow||06-07-2001||07:08 PM||||On mine I just cut it off.  Right as it started to become even with the pipe.  I started doing it with a hacksaw till my buddy came over with a power saw, and boom in less then a couple of minutes it was cut.  The pipe I am using is from Rodney Dickman.  I got the pipe on and now that Ed has it he is getting it welded for me.<P>                              Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Seanh||06-07-2001||07:13 PM||||Yeah, thats pretty much what I am going to do. Mine has already been cut off, and is now clamped on.<P>Getting a little off my topic, but MooCow, ED has your car now? I was just curious because I read a while back you had some head gasket trouble and would not be able to get the car back to the Fiero Factory. So whats going on with it now? Are you still selling it, or is Ed repairing it? Just curious.||||reg||1
Z||000015||MooCow||06-07-2001||10:14 PM||||Turns out it was never the headgaskets at all.  Boy do I hate my mechanics around here.  I got it on a semi on Monday and Ed got it Wednesday.  Turns out there was to much oil in the sending unit and something with the gas.  All I have to do now is find a way to get it home and Im all set. No I plan on keeping it.  After thinking long and hard about it I decided I better keep it.<BR>Good luck at your catilytic converter.<P>                              Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||10
